# FastAPI Route Development Rules

## 1. Synchronous vs Asynchronous Handlers
- **Always use `def` (synchronous)** when calling ZeroC Ice RPC methods (e.g. `meta.getServer()`, `server.isRunning()`).
- ZeroC Ice uses blocking socket I/O. FastAPI runs synchronous `def` routes in a threadpool worker, avoiding blocking the async event loop.
- Only use `async def` for pure I/O endpoints that do NOT interact with ZeroC Ice (e.g., simple in-memory health checks).

## 2. Route Registration & Ordering
- Place **static routes before dynamic parameterized routes**:
  - `GET /servers/version`
  - `POST /servers/deleteServers`
  - `GET /servers/userCount`
  - Must all appear BEFORE `GET /servers/{id}`.
- Follow RESTful resource conventions:
  - Collection: `GET /servers`, `POST /servers`
  - Item: `GET /servers/{id}`, `DELETE /servers/{id}`, `PATCH /servers/{id}`
  - Actions: `POST /servers/{id}/start`, `POST /servers/{id}/stop`, `POST /servers/{id}/restart`
  - Logs: `GET /servers/{id}/logs`

## 3. Decorator & Error Handling
- Always decorate endpoints that call Ice with `@handle_ice_errors` from `app.exceptions`.
- Explicitly set `response_model` on all endpoints for OpenAPI documentation.
- Raise `HTTPException(status_code=404, detail="Server ID {id} not found")` when an entity does not exist.

## 4. Security & Authentication
- All state-modifying endpoints (`POST`, `PATCH`, `DELETE`) must include:
  `_auth: bool = Depends(verify_api_key)`
- Read-only endpoints (`GET`) do not require authentication unless specified by configuration.

